{
  "_comment": [
    "Role-scoped draft archetypes. Keyed role -> archetype -> champion ids.",
    "",
    "A champion is a different thing in different lanes \u2014 Camille top is a split",
    "pusher, Camille support is a playmaker \u2014 so this is keyed on the pair, not",
    "on the champion alone. A champion with no entry for the role it was played",
    "in simply has no archetype, which the UI renders as nothing.",
    "",
    "This is a statement about how a champion is drafted, not something match",
    "results reveal, so it is authored rather than derived. Edit freely: the",
    "lists are the source of truth and nothing else hardcodes a champion name."
  ],
